# 🚀 Application Publishing & Auto-Update Guide

Your `package.json` is now fully configured to use your **Public** GitHub repository (`escape-loop/escloop_gym`) for auto-updating.

Because this repository is public, your users can download updates automatically without needing any special tokens or configuration!

---

## Step 1: Initial Setup & Connecting to GitHub

Run these commands in your terminal to initialize Git and link it to your new repository:

```bash
# 1. Initialize Git
git init

# 2. Add all your files
git add .

# 3. Create your first commit
git commit -m "Initial commit"

# 4. Link it to your GitHub repository
git remote add origin https://github.com/escape-loop/escloop_gym.git

# 5. Push the code
git branch -M main
git push -u origin main
```

---

## Step 2: Creating a GitHub Token (Required for Publishing)

Even though the repo is public, you still need a **GitHub Token** on your development machine to allow `electron-builder` to upload the `.exe` file to your GitHub Releases page.

1. Go to **GitHub.com** -> Click your Profile Picture -> **Settings**.
2. Scroll down to **Developer settings** (bottom left) -> **Personal access tokens** -> **Tokens (classic)**.
3. Click **Generate new token (classic)**.
4. Name it `Escloop Updater`.
5. Check the **`repo`** checkbox.
6. Click Generate, and **copy the token** (it starts with `ghp_`).

**Add the token to your computer:**
*   Open your Windows Search bar and type **"Environment Variables"**.
*   Click **"Edit the system environment variables"**.
*   Click the **"Environment Variables..."** button at the bottom.
*   Under "User variables", click **New**.
*   Variable name: `GH_TOKEN`
*   Variable value: *(paste your token here)*
*   Click OK, and **restart your terminal/VSCode** for it to take effect.

---

## Step 3: Pushing an Update (Your New Workflow)

Whenever you make changes to the code and want to push a new update to all your users, follow these 3 steps:

### 1. Increase the Version Number
Open `package.json` and change the `"version"` field. 
*(Example: change `"1.0.0"` to `"1.0.1"`)*

### 2. Push Source Code to GitHub
Save your code to GitHub:
```bash
git add .
git commit -m "Description of changes"
git push
```

### 3. Build & Publish the `.exe`
Run this command. It will compile your React client, build the Windows Installer, and upload the `.exe` directly to your GitHub Releases:
```bash
npm run dist -- -p always
```

---

## Step 4: Users Receive the Update!
When any user opens the Escloop Gym Manager, the app will:
1. Contact GitHub and see that a new version is available.
2. Download the update silently in the background.
3. Automatically install the new version the next time they open the app!
